OL,3,GNEWSAMum upset by 'heartless' decision
OL,4,Aas daughter can no longer have
OL,5,Awheelchair
OL,6,
OL,7,FA mother has criticised the "heartless"
OL,8,Fdecision to no longer allow her
OL,9,Fautistic daughter to have a wheelchair.
OL,11,FAlex Doyle's seven-year-old daughter
OL,12,FRemi used a wheelchair for the last
OL,13,Ffive years but she was told by bosses
OL,14,Ffrom Mersey Care NHS Foundation Trust
OL,15,Fthat she is no longer eligible for one.
OL,17,FThe 37-year-old, from Knowsley, said
OL,18,Fher daughter needs the chair as she has
OL,19,F"no sense of danger" and would run into
OL,20,Fthe road without it. It also acts as a
OL,21,F"safe haven" for her in crowds, she
OL,22,Fsaid.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,405,400,260,160,0,100
